WEBVTT

00:00:14.448 --> 00:00:18.104
And repairs are complete.
Should we head back in?

00:00:18.148 --> 00:00:21.499
Wow, would you look at that?

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.242
Captain, we just received
a distress call

00:00:25.285 --> 00:00:26.504
from the &lt;i&gt;Bakersfield.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:26.547 --> 00:00:28.419
They're caught in
a temporal causality loop.

00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:30.638
Wait a minute, I'm getting
the same distress call again.

00:00:30.682 --> 00:00:32.379
Hold on. And now again.

00:00:32.423 --> 00:00:33.946
Sounds like a time loop
all right.

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:35.643
We'd better hurry.
Warp me.

00:00:35.687 --> 00:00:37.254
A view like this
makes you realize

00:00:37.297 --> 00:00:38.820
it doesn't matter what deck
you work on.

00:00:38.864 --> 00:00:40.300
We're all in it together.

00:00:42.781 --> 00:00:44.174
And they left us.

00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:46.001
They left us.
How much oxygen do we have?

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.525
A lot, a little?
Ballpark?

00:00:47.568 --> 00:00:49.135
Oh, I'm sure they'll turn back
at any second

00:00:49.179 --> 00:00:51.833
and we'll have a good laugh
about it.

00:00:58.362 --> 00:01:01.365
See, guys? We're laughing.
Ha-ha-ha-ha.

00:02:14.786 --> 00:02:17.963
There we go, nothing a little
lung rejuvenation won't fix.

00:02:18.006 --> 00:02:19.356
See? You're fine.

00:02:19.399 --> 00:02:20.879
Oh, yeah, act like
it's not a big deal

00:02:20.922 --> 00:02:23.142
that you left us to
die in the void.

00:02:23.186 --> 00:02:24.665
This all could have been
avoided if you'd

00:02:24.709 --> 00:02:27.320
followed protocol and signed out
your magnet boots.

00:02:27.364 --> 00:02:28.582
Or maybe that wouldn't have
even mattered

00:02:28.626 --> 00:02:31.150
since lower decks
are so expendable to you.

00:02:31.194 --> 00:02:34.719
Ridiculous! We're all equals
on this ship, right?

00:02:34.762 --> 00:02:36.982
- Uh, they sleep in a hallway.
- Oh.

00:02:37.025 --> 00:02:38.331
I'm not going to argue
with you, Beckett.

00:02:38.375 --> 00:02:40.159
I have to make impossible
life-and-death decisions

00:02:40.203 --> 00:02:41.639
every day.

00:02:41.682 --> 00:02:44.163
Yeah, no kidding, it's always &lt;i&gt;
our&lt;/i&gt; life or death.

00:02:44.207 --> 00:02:46.992
Ditch the attitude!
A Starfleet drill instructor

00:02:47.035 --> 00:02:49.429
is going to be
testing the crew later today,

00:02:49.473 --> 00:02:52.258
and I don't need you
messing up our score

00:02:52.302 --> 00:02:54.173
because you've got
a chip on your shoulder.

00:02:54.217 --> 00:02:56.001
Oh, great, yeah, well, I hope
one of the drills

00:02:56.044 --> 00:02:59.483
tests to see if anyone on the
bridge is a giant piece of...

00:02:59.526 --> 00:03:02.442
I heard the drill instructor's
Pandronian.

00:03:02.486 --> 00:03:04.749
You know they can split
their bodies into three parts?

00:03:04.792 --> 00:03:07.969
- I thought I was
a triple threat.
- Ugh.

00:03:08.013 --> 00:03:09.580
Drills, what a waste of time.

00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:12.931
I'd even take real work over
this, like fake pretend work.

00:03:12.974 --> 00:03:15.847
Good morning, &lt;i&gt;Cerritos!&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.936
This one is Shari Yn Yem,

00:03:17.979 --> 00:03:20.547
your friendly Starfleet
drill administrator.

00:03:20.591 --> 00:03:23.724
Like many of you, this one
started from the bottom,

00:03:23.768 --> 00:03:27.467
but with hard work, and plenty
of drills, this one is now...

00:03:27.511 --> 00:03:28.990
at the top!

00:03:31.166 --> 00:03:34.039
These simulator holopods are
each programed

00:03:34.082 --> 00:03:36.607
with individualized drills
based on

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.784
situations other Starfleet crews
have experienced.

00:03:39.827 --> 00:03:42.874
Every pod has a certain amount
of points you can earn

00:03:42.917 --> 00:03:44.310
for doing a good job.

00:03:44.354 --> 00:03:46.530
Everyone's score is displayed
right here,

00:03:46.573 --> 00:03:49.533
so you can see how you stack up
against your fellow crew.

00:03:49.576 --> 00:03:52.100
Almost seems unfair to
make them compete with us.

00:03:52.144 --> 00:03:53.841
Gonna be a piece of cake.

00:03:53.885 --> 00:03:55.669
This one will be
flipping your ranks.

00:03:55.713 --> 00:03:59.325
Low-level officers will be
given command of the bridge,

00:03:59.369 --> 00:04:02.633
while senior officers will be
placed on the lower decks!

00:04:02.676 --> 00:04:04.330
Excuse me. What?!

00:04:04.374 --> 00:04:07.115
Well, there's no better way to
evaluate a crew's readiness

00:04:07.159 --> 00:04:08.813
than from the bottom up,
Captain.

00:04:08.856 --> 00:04:11.990
- Or should I say, Ensign?

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:15.254
Oh, yeah! This rules!

00:04:15.298 --> 00:04:17.387
I get to be senior
medical officer!

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.085
Ooh, baby, I'm chief engineer!

00:04:20.128 --> 00:04:21.216
Good day to you,
Captain Boimler.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.871
Good day to you,
Captain Mariner.

00:04:23.915 --> 00:04:25.525
They actually think they're
going to be able

00:04:25.569 --> 00:04:27.048
to handle our jobs?

00:04:27.092 --> 00:04:28.572
This is gonna be rich.

00:04:28.615 --> 00:04:30.400
All right, deck 12,
follow the yellow line.

00:04:30.443 --> 00:04:32.097
Move it along, lower decks.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.577
- Aw, son of a...

00:04:35.361 --> 00:04:38.059
- All right, let's get into it.

00:04:38.103 --> 00:04:40.018
I wanna rack up some points
early so I can spend

00:04:40.061 --> 00:04:42.455
the rest of the day soaking
in my commander's tub.

00:04:42.499 --> 00:04:45.632
&lt;i&gt;Mirror Universe Encounter.
- Mirror universe?&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:45.676 --> 00:04:49.723
This is easy. Yeah. I can
pretend to be evil. Ha-ha-ha-ha!

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:52.335
&lt;i&gt;As captain, you must infiltrate
the Terran Empire&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:52.378 --> 00:04:55.207
&lt;i&gt;and find a way back
to your own dimension.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:57.818
Long live the Empire.

00:04:57.862 --> 00:05:01.431
I love to hate.
Whattup, Migleemo?

00:05:01.474 --> 00:05:03.911
- Yikes.

00:05:03.955 --> 00:05:08.263
Ugh, nothing makes me hornier
than torturing someone.

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:09.787
I'm horny all the time.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.442
And being horny always gets me
in the mood to torture.

00:05:12.485 --> 00:05:14.922
You can lose a whole day
to that cycle.

00:05:14.966 --> 00:05:17.925
Okay, screw finding an ally,
let's take over the ship and see

00:05:17.969 --> 00:05:19.971
if we can dismantle the
Terran Empire from the inside.

00:05:20.014 --> 00:05:22.800
&lt;i&gt;Deviation from mission
parameters&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:22.843 --> 00:05:24.105
&lt;i&gt;results in loss of points.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:24.149 --> 00:05:25.368
Okay, all right, I get it, yeah.

00:05:25.411 --> 00:05:27.152
You're not exactly rewarding
creativity.

00:05:27.195 --> 00:05:29.328
Who dareth bump into me?!

00:05:29.372 --> 00:05:32.200
Oh, I dareth.
I double-dog dareth.

00:05:32.244 --> 00:05:33.680
Ah! Ooh!

00:05:33.724 --> 00:05:35.378
Okay, good. Just checking.

00:05:37.162 --> 00:05:40.078
I need to figure out a way to
impress or kill the captain

00:05:40.121 --> 00:05:42.385
so I can get on
a more sinister ship.

00:05:44.604 --> 00:05:46.171
Long live the Empire.

00:05:46.214 --> 00:05:48.434
Long live the-- wait,
did you just salute me

00:05:48.478 --> 00:05:49.653
with your left hand?

00:05:49.696 --> 00:05:51.394
Our Mariner is right-handed.

00:05:51.437 --> 00:05:54.440
Uh, no, I just,
uh, I strained this shoulder

00:05:54.484 --> 00:05:55.876
flogging a Vulcan.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:58.444
Get her!

00:05:58.488 --> 00:06:00.620
- Whoa!

00:06:03.449 --> 00:06:04.929
&lt;i&gt;Fail.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:04.972 --> 00:06:06.931
- Damn.
- Don't worry, Commander.

00:06:06.974 --> 00:06:08.541
You'll have other opportunities

00:06:08.585 --> 00:06:11.022
to get a-head.

00:06:11.065 --> 00:06:13.851
- That's one of my faves.

00:06:13.894 --> 00:06:17.028
&lt;i&gt;Medical ethics.
Chief medical officer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:17.071 --> 00:06:20.161
&lt;i&gt;navigate a paralyzed Klingon's request&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:20.205 --> 00:06:21.598
&lt;i&gt;for an honorable death.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:21.641 --> 00:06:23.208
Oh, uh, okay.

00:06:23.251 --> 00:06:24.862
You must help me kill myself.

00:06:24.905 --> 00:06:26.951
I broke my back
picking up a peanut.

00:06:26.994 --> 00:06:29.475
Well, as head of medical,
I'm not supposed to do any harm.

00:06:29.519 --> 00:06:30.607
- Huh?

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:31.608
&lt;i&gt;Points deducted.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:31.651 --> 00:06:34.001
What? Oh.
I guess in that case,

00:06:34.045 --> 00:06:36.700
let's send you off
to Sto-vo-kor.

00:06:36.743 --> 00:06:39.267
No! You must use
my ceremonial blade!

00:06:39.311 --> 00:06:41.531
Ew. No. It'll be quick
and painless this way.

00:06:41.574 --> 00:06:43.141
&lt;i&gt;Points deducted.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:43.184 --> 00:06:45.317
Huh? I-I gotta hurt him?

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.275
You refuse to honor my culture?!

00:06:47.319 --> 00:06:49.103
Oh, no, no, sir,
I-I wanna kill you, I...

00:06:49.147 --> 00:06:51.541
Just give me the knife. Aah!

00:06:51.584 --> 00:06:53.891
Good God, what did you do?

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:55.153
This Klingon isn't dead.

00:06:55.196 --> 00:06:57.024
I-I was trying to save him?

00:06:57.068 --> 00:06:59.679
- What? Come on. Come on.
- Faster. Kill me. Kill!

00:06:59.723 --> 00:07:01.899
We have to get this warrior
an honorable death, stat!

00:07:01.942 --> 00:07:05.555
- Get me 300cc's of
any type of poison.
- I have to die!

00:07:05.598 --> 00:07:08.296
They have giant hearts,
so many backup organs.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:11.691
Sir, it's done. There's
nothing else we can do.

00:07:11.735 --> 00:07:13.650
Damn it. Call it.

00:07:13.693 --> 00:07:15.956
Time of life, 0900.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.089
No!

00:07:18.132 --> 00:07:19.786
Sorry. &lt;i&gt;
Fail.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:25.139 --> 00:07:27.098
&lt;i&gt;Old West planet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:27.141 --> 00:07:29.666
&lt;i&gt;As captain, you must survive
a lawless frontier town&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:29.709 --> 00:07:31.842
&lt;i&gt;in Earth's 19th century.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:31.885 --> 00:07:33.626
&lt;i&gt;But beware, for you are
a wanted man...&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:35.498
Yeah, yeah, I get it.
Trapped in cowboy land.

00:07:35.541 --> 00:07:37.151
It's a Starfleet classic.
Yeehaw.

00:07:37.195 --> 00:07:39.197
- Just gotta find the saloon...

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.069
What? I haven't even done
anything creative.

00:07:42.113 --> 00:07:44.202
Oh, we have to ride
the horses. Okay.

00:07:44.245 --> 00:07:46.334
Seems kinda like a narrow
parameter for a drill.

00:07:48.119 --> 00:07:51.252
Calm down, horses love me;
I'm a maverick.

00:07:51.296 --> 00:07:53.994
Whoa! Aah!

00:07:54.038 --> 00:07:56.736
Help! Aah! Ow! Bad horse.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:57.824
&lt;i&gt;Fail.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:59.565 --> 00:08:02.220
Mm-mm-mm.

00:08:03.482 --> 00:08:05.919
&lt;i&gt;The Good of the Many.
Chief Engineer,&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:05.963 --> 00:08:08.443
&lt;i&gt;enter the chamber
and fix the warp core breach&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:09.793
&lt;i&gt;to save the ship.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:09.836 --> 00:08:11.925
- Okey dokey.
- Sir, the radiation!

00:08:11.969 --> 00:08:13.274
You can't go in there!

00:08:13.318 --> 00:08:16.451
I have to, son.
I'm chief engineer.

00:08:16.495 --> 00:08:18.932
- Ooh, that sounds so good.

00:08:18.976 --> 00:08:22.283
Ow! Hot! Uh, maybe if I...
Aah! Frickin' radiation.

00:08:22.327 --> 00:08:23.763
&lt;i&gt;Warp core breach imminent.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:23.807 --> 00:08:25.548
I know, computer.
But how am I supposed to-- Ow!

00:08:25.591 --> 00:08:28.333
Wow, this really shouldn't
be that hard.

00:08:28.376 --> 00:08:30.248
Shut up, Ensign!
Wait, my boot.

00:08:30.291 --> 00:08:31.597
&lt;i&gt;Warp core critical.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:31.641 --> 00:08:34.208
Ha-ha!
Come on, come on.

00:08:34.252 --> 00:08:35.949
Got it!

00:08:39.039 --> 00:08:40.563
&lt;i&gt;- Fail.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:43.827 --> 00:08:45.785
&lt;i&gt;-Borg Encounter.
- Uh, could you be&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:45.829 --> 00:08:47.178
a little more
specific than that?

00:08:47.221 --> 00:08:48.701
&lt;i&gt;Resist the Borg.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:48.745 --> 00:08:50.224
Okay, you know what,
that's fine. I've read literally

00:08:50.268 --> 00:08:53.010
everything about the Borg;
I've got this.

00:08:53.053 --> 00:08:55.578
Wow, the detail on this
is amazing.

00:08:55.621 --> 00:08:59.103
We are Borg.
Resistance is futile.

00:08:59.146 --> 00:09:01.105
Whoa, this is so cool!

00:09:01.148 --> 00:09:02.889
Oh, sorry. Please, keep going.
Do the thing.

00:09:02.933 --> 00:09:05.805
We will add your biological
distinctiveness to our own.

00:09:05.849 --> 00:09:07.111
You will be assimilated.

00:09:07.154 --> 00:09:08.460
Can't have that.

00:09:12.246 --> 00:09:15.510
All right, can't adjust the
frequency anymore... Yoink.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:18.862
Yeah!

00:09:21.691 --> 00:09:24.650
- Ooh. Oh.

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:30.134
Oh, an escape sphere.

00:09:30.177 --> 00:09:31.483
&lt;i&gt;Woo-hoo!&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:31.526 --> 00:09:33.441
&lt;i&gt;Mission accomplished.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:33.485 --> 00:09:36.662
Oh, yeah! That's right.
Boimler's the Borg man.

00:09:36.706 --> 00:09:39.099
&lt;i&gt;Your score is 79%.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:39.143 --> 00:09:41.754
79? No, no, no, no, no,
I can do better than that.

00:09:41.798 --> 00:09:43.669
- Can I restart? &lt;i&gt;
- If you score below passing,&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:43.713 --> 00:09:45.236
&lt;i&gt;you will be locked out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:45.279 --> 00:09:46.237
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, hit me.

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:47.238
Come on, let's go.

00:09:47.281 --> 00:09:49.980
We are...

00:09:52.983 --> 00:09:55.202
Come on, Borg baby, this time
you're coming with me.

00:09:56.987 --> 00:09:58.292
&lt;i&gt;Woo-hoo!&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:58.336 --> 00:10:00.164
&lt;i&gt;83%.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:00.207 --> 00:10:01.731
I can do better.

00:10:05.909 --> 00:10:06.823
&lt;i&gt;Woo-hoo!&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:08.215 --> 00:10:09.564
&lt;i&gt;84%.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:13.133
Do it again. Hit me!

00:10:13.177 --> 00:10:14.439
Naked Time?

00:10:14.482 --> 00:10:16.049
&lt;i&gt;As captain,
you must save your crew,&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:16.093 --> 00:10:17.442
&lt;i&gt;who are under the influence
of a virus&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:17.485 --> 00:10:20.140
&lt;i&gt;that reduces their inhibitions.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:20.184 --> 00:10:22.621
Oh, no, this is
that disease that made everyone

00:10:22.665 --> 00:10:24.188
fight and have sex
all over the place.

00:10:24.231 --> 00:10:27.582
&lt;i&gt;Can you resist your own
temptations and save the ship?&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:29.933
- Come on, girl. Last one.
You got this.

00:10:29.976 --> 00:10:32.849
Wow, everyone's very slick
and sliding around.

00:10:32.892 --> 00:10:35.721
Keep your hands to yourselves.
Hey, that's an anus!

00:10:36.896 --> 00:10:38.724
- Oh.
Ooh.

00:10:38.768 --> 00:10:40.465
Oh!

00:10:40.508 --> 00:10:42.902
I can't tell where
I end and you begin.

00:10:42.946 --> 00:10:45.339
It's naked time!

00:10:45.383 --> 00:10:47.690
Oh, fail me, fail me!
Seriously,

00:10:47.733 --> 00:10:49.692
why is this drill still going?
Fail me.

00:10:49.735 --> 00:10:51.432
Put me back in the Western!

00:11:00.615 --> 00:11:03.531
Ugh, I failed every
single drill.

00:11:03.575 --> 00:11:05.403
At least you weren't
responsible for the destruction

00:11:05.446 --> 00:11:06.752
of a whole ship.

00:11:06.796 --> 00:11:08.362
All those life-and-death
decisions,

00:11:08.406 --> 00:11:10.974
I honestly don't know how
Dr. T'Ana does it every day.

00:11:11.017 --> 00:11:13.498
Mmm. Computer, what is this?

00:11:13.541 --> 00:11:15.413
&lt;i&gt;That is pesto.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:15.456 --> 00:11:16.980
Where's Boimler? He lives
for this kind of spread.

00:11:17.023 --> 00:11:18.808
Last I heard, he was still
doing his drill.

00:11:18.851 --> 00:11:20.984
Yeah, right. I bet he
bombed out just like us

00:11:21.027 --> 00:11:22.725
and he doesn't want to admit it.

00:11:22.768 --> 00:11:24.335
-♪

00:11:26.163 --> 00:11:27.251
We got your signal.
How were you able to...

00:11:27.294 --> 00:11:28.948
Just fly.

00:11:31.211 --> 00:11:33.605
&lt;i&gt;-94%.
- Again.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:33.648 --> 00:11:35.825
&lt;i&gt;Your score is already
in the top ten...&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:35.868 --> 00:11:37.087
I said again!

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.568
It hurts me to say this, but...

00:11:40.612 --> 00:11:43.920
maybe the bridge crew's jobs are
actually harder than we thought.

00:11:43.963 --> 00:11:45.922
Yeah, well, I'm sure right now
they're finding out

00:11:45.965 --> 00:11:48.576
just how hard it is to
do our jobs, too.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:53.843
I almost forgot how easy being
a lower-decker is.

00:11:53.886 --> 00:11:56.715
All I did was stand in the
back of a banquet all day.

00:11:56.759 --> 00:11:58.499
I just waited in
the transporter bay

00:11:58.543 --> 00:12:00.240
in case anybody
needed to be transported.

00:12:00.284 --> 00:12:02.155
Why did we ever rank up again?

00:12:02.199 --> 00:12:04.027
So what if their showers
are a little cramped,

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:05.332
or their replicators
can only make

00:12:05.376 --> 00:12:07.465
one slice of pizza at a time?

00:12:07.508 --> 00:12:09.206
A small price to pay
for no worries

00:12:09.249 --> 00:12:10.816
and no responsibilities.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:13.340
Even these close quarters
don't bother me.

00:12:13.384 --> 00:12:16.866
Mmm.

00:12:16.909 --> 00:12:19.825
Yep, I could get used
to this easy life.

00:12:21.827 --> 00:12:24.177
- Ow! What the [bleep]?!

00:12:27.702 --> 00:12:29.052
&lt;i&gt;Klingon Encounter.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:29.095 --> 00:12:32.055
Really? I think I know how
to handle one of those.

00:12:32.098 --> 00:12:35.493
&lt;i&gt;Ensigns, your mission is to
support your commanders.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.627
Stop goofing around, Ensigns!
The ship's under attack!

00:12:39.671 --> 00:12:41.891
- What happened?
- Don't worry about it.
Get to work.

00:12:41.934 --> 00:12:44.197
These crates aren't gonna
stack themselves.

00:12:44.241 --> 00:12:47.157
Really? There are Klingons on
the other side of the hull,

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.072
and this is our job?

00:12:49.115 --> 00:12:50.595
Aw, son of a...

00:12:51.814 --> 00:12:53.467
If they wanted us
to stack these,

00:12:53.511 --> 00:12:55.513
then why are they shaped
like this?!

00:12:55.556 --> 00:12:56.731
Quick! Have you seen
a Q come through here?

00:12:56.775 --> 00:12:58.777
- Q is on the ship?
- Forget I said anything.

00:12:58.821 --> 00:13:01.214
Commander, wait.
We're Starfleet officers.

00:13:01.258 --> 00:13:02.694
We can help you,
just tell us what's...

00:13:02.737 --> 00:13:05.392
The Jem'Hadar?
Get to battle stations!

00:13:05.436 --> 00:13:06.741
Damn it!

00:13:06.785 --> 00:13:08.352
Aha! I got it.

00:13:10.745 --> 00:13:12.312
&lt;i&gt;Failed!&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:19.450
Now that both sides have been
put through individual tests,

00:13:19.493 --> 00:13:22.845
your last drill will be

00:13:22.888 --> 00:13:24.150
a simulated experience

00:13:24.194 --> 00:13:26.544
that uses your real bridge.

00:13:26.587 --> 00:13:29.460
The true test of a crew is
seeing how you can

00:13:29.503 --> 00:13:31.027
unite as a single team.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:33.420
"Steal the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos
from spacedock&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:33.464 --> 00:13:35.335
and use it to save Spock
on the Genesis planet."

00:13:35.379 --> 00:13:37.685
- Okay, yeah.
- An oldie but a goodie.

00:13:37.729 --> 00:13:40.601
And just what do you think
you're doing, Ensign Freeman?

00:13:40.645 --> 00:13:42.516
Force of habit.

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:44.779
All right, look alive, people.
Yeoman Ransom,

00:13:44.823 --> 00:13:46.912
let's get some fresh coffee
on deck.

00:13:46.956 --> 00:13:48.392
Yes, sir.

00:13:48.435 --> 00:13:50.524
Ensign Freeman, full thrusters,
take us out.

00:13:50.568 --> 00:13:53.745
Aye, Captain.
90 seconds to spacedock.

00:13:55.355 --> 00:13:57.009
Ensign Shaxs,
what are you doing?

00:13:57.053 --> 00:13:59.098
Requesting permission to
stretch, Captain.

00:13:59.142 --> 00:14:02.232
My back's killing me
from sleeping in those bunks.

00:14:02.275 --> 00:14:05.104
Oh, it's naked time!

00:14:05.148 --> 00:14:07.541
Ugh! No.
Stop that. Stop now.

00:14:07.585 --> 00:14:08.629
Geez, what's gotten into you?

00:14:08.673 --> 00:14:10.153
It's-it's just something

00:14:10.196 --> 00:14:11.458
I'm remembering from the drills.

00:14:11.502 --> 00:14:12.590
The one where you couldn't even

00:14:12.633 --> 00:14:13.765
get on a horse?

00:14:13.808 --> 00:14:15.114
How do you know about that?

00:14:15.158 --> 00:14:16.899
The drills are public, Beckett.

00:14:16.942 --> 00:14:18.291
I watched the playback.

00:14:18.335 --> 00:14:20.728
I'm just saying,
two and a half years of lessons

00:14:20.772 --> 00:14:23.122
- and that's what you had
to show for it?

00:14:23.166 --> 00:14:24.384
Congratulations, Ensign.

00:14:24.428 --> 00:14:25.951
You've earned yourself
a trip to the brig.

00:14:25.995 --> 00:14:27.257
- I've never been sent
to the brig.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.433
- Well, now you have.
- On what grounds?

00:14:29.476 --> 00:14:30.608
On my grounds!

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.742
Beckett,
I am speaking!

00:14:34.786 --> 00:14:37.267
Captain, did you want
your coffee with cream or...

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:39.486
Dang.
That's gotta be a record.

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:41.227
Actually, it is.

00:14:43.795 --> 00:14:46.232
I can't believe we didn't even
make it out of the spacedock.

00:14:46.276 --> 00:14:48.408
There's not even a numerical
score for that.

00:14:48.452 --> 00:14:50.019
Just "incomplete."

00:14:50.062 --> 00:14:51.977
Oof, somehow that feels worse.

00:14:52.021 --> 00:14:53.674
- I guess I...
- You know I...

00:14:53.718 --> 00:14:55.372
- Oh, you go.
- No, no, no, you.

00:14:55.415 --> 00:14:57.983
You know, it's been so
long since I've been an ensign,

00:14:58.027 --> 00:15:00.464
I forgot how hard it can be
when you're not in the loop.

00:15:00.507 --> 00:15:04.424
In a lot of ways, taking orders
is the more challenging job.

00:15:04.468 --> 00:15:06.600
That's nice to hear, but ditto.

00:15:06.644 --> 00:15:08.211
Commander-level stuff is hard.

00:15:08.254 --> 00:15:10.822
Just the constant tightrope
walk of protocol.

00:15:10.865 --> 00:15:12.302
Not worth the pesto.

00:15:12.345 --> 00:15:13.651
Guess the carpet's always grayer

00:15:13.694 --> 00:15:16.219
- on the other side of the ship.
- Big-time.

00:15:16.262 --> 00:15:19.004
Do they
know what "stacked" means?

00:15:19.048 --> 00:15:21.093
We're stacking
for what reason?

00:15:21.137 --> 00:15:23.052
Hold on.

00:15:23.095 --> 00:15:25.141
That's what this has all
been about.

00:15:25.184 --> 00:15:26.969
That drills consultant
made us suffer

00:15:27.012 --> 00:15:28.579
through all of this crap

00:15:28.622 --> 00:15:31.060
just so we'd understand
what the other ranks go through.

00:15:31.103 --> 00:15:32.583
That's the actual drill here.

00:15:32.626 --> 00:15:34.150
Ugh, you're right!

00:15:34.193 --> 00:15:36.282
Where is that
tri-bodied little trickster?

00:15:36.326 --> 00:15:38.023
I want to shake her hand.

00:15:39.764 --> 00:15:41.461
Yo, Shari Yingo Yango,

00:15:41.505 --> 00:15:43.376
- we figured you out, girl.
- You did?

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:46.336
Yeah, these drills were
secretly about team building.

00:15:46.379 --> 00:15:48.816
You came in to make us
appreciate each other more.

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:51.515
And it worked! Thanks to you,
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; crew will

00:15:51.558 --> 00:15:53.343
move forward with
greater empathy

00:15:53.386 --> 00:15:55.910
and a deeper
appreciation for each other.

00:15:59.697 --> 00:16:03.875
Oh, no, you won't be moving
forward at all.

00:16:10.577 --> 00:16:11.578
- What are you--

00:16:11.622 --> 00:16:13.972
what is she laughing about?

00:16:14.016 --> 00:16:15.191
Oh, come on.

00:16:15.234 --> 00:16:16.888
Your drills scores
are well below failing.

00:16:16.931 --> 00:16:18.977
Once they're submitted,
Starfleet Command will

00:16:19.021 --> 00:16:21.893
relegate and reassign
this entire crew.

00:16:21.936 --> 00:16:23.460
So this wasn't about teamwork?

00:16:23.503 --> 00:16:25.244
Teamwork? No.

00:16:25.288 --> 00:16:26.811
This was about
saving my job.

00:16:26.854 --> 00:16:29.335
The bigger ships always passed
my drills with no problem.

00:16:29.379 --> 00:16:30.945
It was starting to seem
like we didn't

00:16:30.989 --> 00:16:32.295
need a drills program at all.

00:16:32.338 --> 00:16:34.297
This one needed a crew
to fall short

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.516
to prove the drills were
still valuable,

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:38.649
and, oh, did I find a crew.

00:16:38.692 --> 00:16:40.738
You targeted us for failure?

00:16:40.781 --> 00:16:43.001
This is a ship whose captain
left four ensigns

00:16:43.045 --> 00:16:45.525
on a spacewalk to answer
a distress call.

00:16:45.569 --> 00:16:47.223
It was a pretty safe bet.

00:16:47.266 --> 00:16:50.400
And, of course, it didn't hurt
to goose the drills a bit.

00:16:50.443 --> 00:16:53.229
Oh, I knew it. That mirror
universe drill was rigged.

00:16:53.272 --> 00:16:55.709
They were all rigged!

00:16:55.753 --> 00:16:58.843
And those horses. I would never
get trampled by a horse.

00:16:58.886 --> 00:17:00.236
Oh, actually, no,
the horses weren't rigged.

00:17:00.279 --> 00:17:01.846
I ran out of time.
That one's on you.

00:17:01.889 --> 00:17:02.977
Horses love me. Shut up!

00:17:03.021 --> 00:17:05.110
We won't let you
get away with this.

00:17:05.154 --> 00:17:07.330
&lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; crew, we've got
to do more drills

00:17:07.373 --> 00:17:08.809
- to get our scores up.
- It's too late.

00:17:08.853 --> 00:17:11.116
Once the drills
have been failed,

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.422
you're locked out.

00:17:12.465 --> 00:17:14.902
Soon this one
will submit your final scores

00:17:14.946 --> 00:17:16.556
to Starfleet, and that will be
the end of...

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.515
Wait, shut up,
the drills aren't over.

00:17:18.558 --> 00:17:20.256
- One is still active.
- What? Which one?

00:17:20.299 --> 00:17:21.692
- It's Boimler!
- How?

00:17:21.735 --> 00:17:23.911
That Borg drill should've
been over hours ago.

00:17:23.955 --> 00:17:25.174
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:17:25.217 --> 00:17:27.350
One passing score will make
little difference.

00:17:27.393 --> 00:17:30.701
- If the drills aren't
finished...
- Our scores aren't final!

00:17:30.744 --> 00:17:32.224
Boimler, can you hear me?

00:17:32.268 --> 00:17:34.618
Hey, Mariner, I was just about
to close out this drill.

00:17:34.661 --> 00:17:36.794
- I finally got a perfect... &lt;i&gt;
Don't you finish
that drill, Ensign.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:36.837 --> 00:17:38.100
&lt;i&gt;That's an order!&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:38.143 --> 00:17:39.753
Captain, but I beat
the Borg Queen in chess,

00:17:39.797 --> 00:17:42.016
- and I taught her empathy. &lt;i&gt;
- Just stay in that drill!&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:44.106
The crew is counting on you.

00:17:44.149 --> 00:17:45.890
Yeah, Shari Bing Bang
is trying to screw us,

00:17:45.933 --> 00:17:47.761
&lt;i&gt;but she can't
until your drill is over.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:47.805 --> 00:17:49.589
&lt;i&gt;-Just keep Borging!
- I'm on it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:49.633 --> 00:17:52.201
Resistance is futile.

00:17:52.244 --> 00:17:53.680
Aw, man.

00:17:53.724 --> 00:17:56.292
You know you've already lost,
right?

00:17:56.335 --> 00:17:58.598
All you're doing is
torturing that young officer.

00:17:58.642 --> 00:18:00.383
He'll be fine.
He's one of our best.

00:18:00.426 --> 00:18:02.167
- He is?
- None of you are the best.

00:18:02.211 --> 00:18:04.038
You're on
a California Class ship.

00:18:04.082 --> 00:18:06.563
Most of the Federation
doesn't even know you exist.

00:18:06.606 --> 00:18:08.521
The smaller the ship,
the tougher the crew.

00:18:08.565 --> 00:18:10.262
Oh, please, face the truth.

00:18:10.306 --> 00:18:11.698
This one's made the drills.

00:18:11.742 --> 00:18:13.918
This one's read all about life
on starships.

00:18:13.961 --> 00:18:17.008
Exactly. You've read
how to work in space,

00:18:17.051 --> 00:18:19.967
but have you ever been in a real
life-or-death situation?

00:18:20.011 --> 00:18:22.405
- That doesn't matter.
- It's about to.

00:18:22.448 --> 00:18:24.755
Captain on deck!
Real captain.

00:18:24.798 --> 00:18:28.150
Ensign Tendi, run a long-range
scan for any potentially

00:18:28.193 --> 00:18:29.760
hazardous anomalies
in this system.

00:18:29.803 --> 00:18:31.414
Yes, sir. Is this a new drill?

00:18:31.457 --> 00:18:33.372
Oh, no, this is real.

00:18:33.416 --> 00:18:35.548
What is that supposed to mean?

00:18:35.592 --> 00:18:38.247
All right, let's see, we've got
a tetryon wormhole,

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:39.900
chroniton radiation stream.

00:18:39.944 --> 00:18:41.206
Ooh, a loner crystalline entity,

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:43.948
a crystalline entity
consuming a rogue planet,

00:18:43.991 --> 00:18:45.993
a couple crystalline entities
getting frisky-- huh.

00:18:46.037 --> 00:18:47.560
Lots of, lots of
crystalline entities today.

00:18:47.604 --> 00:18:49.736
Must be crystalline entity
season or something.

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:51.521
Ensign, set an intercept course

00:18:51.564 --> 00:18:53.044
for one of those
crystalline entities.

00:18:53.087 --> 00:18:54.785
- Warp four.
- Aye aye, Captain!

00:18:54.828 --> 00:18:57.744
"The Crystalline Entity"
is drill number 89.

00:18:57.788 --> 00:18:59.442
A classic. Can't wait.

00:19:00.486 --> 00:19:02.314
Oh, God. Oh, God. Oh, no!

00:19:02.358 --> 00:19:03.837
No, no, no, no, no.

00:19:03.881 --> 00:19:05.665
Come on, Mariner, whatever
you're doing up there, hurry!

00:19:05.709 --> 00:19:07.580
Aah! Borg Queen!

00:19:11.105 --> 00:19:13.543
Uh, how-how's the empathy?

00:19:13.586 --> 00:19:15.501
We were able to assimilate it.

00:19:15.545 --> 00:19:18.809
No, no, no, no, no, my score!

00:19:20.854 --> 00:19:22.769
Captain, we've reached
the crystalline entity.

00:19:22.813 --> 00:19:25.903
It appears to be feeding on
unstable nebula radiation.

00:19:25.946 --> 00:19:28.253
Oh, my, it's bigger
than this one thought.

00:19:28.297 --> 00:19:29.515
Unstable, huh?

00:19:29.559 --> 00:19:31.604
Seems like something
we should investigate.

00:19:31.648 --> 00:19:33.040
Shields up, take us in.

00:19:33.084 --> 00:19:34.825
What? No! In my drill,
you're never supposed to...

00:19:34.868 --> 00:19:36.130
This isn't a drill.

00:19:41.658 --> 00:19:43.399
Shields holding, Captain,

00:19:43.442 --> 00:19:46.010
but I'm reading transphasic
energy within the perimeter.

00:19:46.053 --> 00:19:49.100
That's a new one.
Let's get a closer look!

00:19:49.143 --> 00:19:52.321
No! We don't know
the effect of--

00:19:52.364 --> 00:19:53.800
Controls are getting choppy.

00:19:53.844 --> 00:19:55.802
&lt;i&gt;We're caught
in an electromagnetic&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:55.846 --> 00:19:58.718
resonance belt.
I think we're in trouble!

00:19:58.762 --> 00:20:00.851
This is not good!

00:20:00.894 --> 00:20:03.114
Whoa!

00:20:07.945 --> 00:20:11.731
Mariner, I really need
to get out of here. Like now!

00:20:11.775 --> 00:20:12.993
- Ooh.

00:20:13.037 --> 00:20:14.168
Kinda tickles.

00:20:14.212 --> 00:20:15.909
A remarkable creature.

00:20:15.953 --> 00:20:18.608
Your design very nearly passes
as human.

00:20:18.651 --> 00:20:20.392
- I am human.
- Oh!

00:20:20.436 --> 00:20:23.352
Wow. Then you
need to drink more water.

00:20:23.395 --> 00:20:25.092
Your skin is a mess.

00:20:25.136 --> 00:20:28.661
But still, I think I should add
your biological distinctiveness

00:20:28.705 --> 00:20:31.447
to our own;
it's kind of our thing.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:33.187
Are-are you sure?
Because I've got

00:20:33.231 --> 00:20:34.841
hay fever and acid reflux.

00:20:34.885 --> 00:20:38.192
Adding me might result in a net
negative for the collective.

00:20:42.022 --> 00:20:43.937
Oh, this one's gonna puke.

00:20:43.981 --> 00:20:46.940
We need to fire a graviton
pulse to punch a hole out.

00:20:46.984 --> 00:20:50.292
On my mark. Mmm...

00:20:50.335 --> 00:20:52.772
Say "mark"! Say "mark"!
What are you waiting for?!

00:20:52.816 --> 00:20:55.732
Just making sure you're as
scared as you're going to get.

00:20:55.775 --> 00:20:57.342
- You're crazy!
- Mark!

00:20:57.386 --> 00:20:58.300
Full impulse!

00:21:05.394 --> 00:21:08.527
Mariner, find me something else
dangerous to scan.

00:21:08.571 --> 00:21:10.790
I'm in the mood
for a black hole.

00:21:10.834 --> 00:21:12.226
- Why?!
- We're gonna keep doing this

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:14.359
until you change our score.

00:21:14.403 --> 00:21:16.622
There's a black hole feeding on
a temporal rift

00:21:16.666 --> 00:21:18.929
just three systems over.
Lots of time quakes.

00:21:18.972 --> 00:21:21.410
Sounds perfect. Maximum warp.

00:21:23.412 --> 00:21:25.239
You can't blackmail me at
the expense of your crew.

00:21:25.283 --> 00:21:27.111
They do this kind of work
every day.

00:21:27.154 --> 00:21:28.678
You gonna give us
a passing grade,

00:21:28.721 --> 00:21:30.506
or are we just
gonna keep seeking out

00:21:30.549 --> 00:21:32.290
dangerous situations for you

00:21:32.334 --> 00:21:34.379
&lt;i&gt;to see up close?&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:36.816 --> 00:21:39.471
&lt;i&gt;Stop! Stop! We can't!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:41.691 --> 00:21:43.736
Get me out of here!
Get me out of here!

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:47.087
We could do this all day, lady!

00:21:48.393 --> 00:21:52.049
All right, fine.
You win, you win!

00:21:52.092 --> 00:21:54.356
There, it's done.
You've passed.

00:21:54.399 --> 00:21:56.183
Mr. Rutherford, stop our spin.

00:21:56.227 --> 00:21:57.141
Aye, Captain.

00:21:58.838 --> 00:22:01.841
What? But the
temporal black hole...

00:22:01.885 --> 00:22:04.627
Well, that was kind of a lie.
It's just a regular black hole.

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:05.932
Yeah, no biggie.

00:22:05.976 --> 00:22:07.238
Which you would have known
if you weren't

00:22:07.281 --> 00:22:09.022
a total fraud.

00:22:09.066 --> 00:22:11.155
I'll be sure to put that
in my report.

00:22:14.114 --> 00:22:16.160
Boimler! We did it.
Hey, it's all good.

00:22:16.203 --> 00:22:17.640
You can exit the drill now.

00:22:17.683 --> 00:22:19.032
Boimler?

00:22:28.477 --> 00:22:30.522
I can him hear him shuffling
around in there.

00:22:30.566 --> 00:22:32.959
Mr. Boimler!
You can come out now.

00:22:33.003 --> 00:22:34.352
You saved the ship!

00:22:34.396 --> 00:22:37.224
There is no Boimler.
I am Excretus of Borg.

00:22:37.268 --> 00:22:38.095
Get him out of there!

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:43.361
Assimilate.
I must assimilate!

00:22:43.405 --> 00:22:46.190
I, uh--
Where am I?

00:22:46.233 --> 00:22:48.322
You're still on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,
Mr. Boimler.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:48.366 --> 00:22:50.542
The crew owes you
a debt of gratitude.

00:22:50.586 --> 00:22:53.327
I was assimilated.
They-they put implants up my...

00:22:53.371 --> 00:22:55.025
Ear is where they put
the implants.

00:22:55.068 --> 00:22:57.854
Right in your ear.
Come on, pal, you need a drink.

00:22:57.897 --> 00:22:59.986
Did I, did I
get my perfect score?

00:23:00.030 --> 00:23:02.249
You sure did.
A hundred percent.

00:23:02.293 --> 00:23:06.036
Hell yeah. Hit me. Hit me again.

00:23:10.170 --> 00:23:12.216
Shari Yn Yem is no longer
working for Starfleet.

00:23:12.259 --> 00:23:16.133
Apparently she stepped down
because of on-the-job stress.

00:23:16.176 --> 00:23:17.874
Feels good,
ruining a jerk's career.

00:23:17.917 --> 00:23:20.616
Agreed. And there was
one thing she did manage

00:23:20.659 --> 00:23:22.139
to teach us today.

00:23:22.182 --> 00:23:24.141
Whoa, new replicator?

00:23:24.184 --> 00:23:26.099
Let's just say we experienced

00:23:26.143 --> 00:23:27.579
what the lower decks
have been eating,

00:23:27.623 --> 00:23:29.929
and noticed it could
use some improvement.

00:23:29.973 --> 00:23:33.629
We updated this one with most of
the senior officer menu codes.

00:23:33.672 --> 00:23:34.847
We get pesto?!

00:23:34.891 --> 00:23:36.327
If you're going to be
facing danger

00:23:36.370 --> 00:23:37.546
on a daily basis,

00:23:37.589 --> 00:23:39.461
might as well get
the good stuff.

00:23:39.504 --> 00:23:41.637
Thanks, guys.
Aw, this is really nice.

00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:42.986
Ooh, ooh, does it make
the lobster mac and cheese

00:23:43.029 --> 00:23:44.248
with the breaded top?

00:23:44.291 --> 00:23:45.467
&lt;i&gt;Sounds like the one thing&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:45.510 --> 00:23:46.642
&lt;i&gt;the Borg left you with&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:46.685 --> 00:23:48.470
&lt;i&gt;-was your appetite.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:48.513 --> 00:23:50.733
&lt;i&gt;They took everything
that I was.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:57.783 --> 00:24:00.786
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:24:52.098 --> 00:24:52.925
Chirp.
